DailyStreak — content provenance and licence scope
==================================================

Licence scope
-------------
The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the source code of this project and the content written for it: the
question text of the scenario decks and of the drill items added since, the English translations, the
difficulty rubric and the documentation.

Question-bank provenance
------------------------
1. AMC 10 concept cards (564) — a rewrite of the knowledge-map section of a third-party study pack
   ("AP-AMC 学习资料"), restructured into question/answer cards for this app. They are study cards, not
   exam questions, and no MAA material is reproduced.
2. AP drill items (600, plus 16 written later) — taken from the same pack, whose own documentation
   states that the files it labels 原创 are AI-generated. They are not College Board questions.
3. Scenario decks (250 items) — written for this repository.
4. English overlay (every card) — translations written for this repository.
5. Verification ledger, difficulty levels, gates and documentation — written for this repository.

What is not in this repository: the study pack itself. Its PDFs, scoring guidelines, score
distributions and study guides stay outside the repository; only the markdown derived from it is
committed, under content/.

Third-party exam material
-------------------------
AMC 10/12 problems are copyright MAA. AP questions are copyright College Board. Neither is included
here, and the MIT licence cannot cover them. If you keep your own copies for personal practice, put
them in `content/local/`: that directory and the file generated from it are gitignored, loaded only at
runtime on your machine, and never published. See docs/local-bank.md.

AI-generated content
--------------------
The app labels provenance on every card and repeats it on the practice screen. Items are marked as
"verified" only when their answer went through an independent recomputation pass; local items are
marked unverified because this repository has not checked them.
